---
import { skills } from '../data/skills';

const stackLine = skills.map((category) => category.items.join(', ')).join(' · ');
---

<section id="about">
  <h2>About</h2>
  <p>
    I started at ULB in 2023, right after my bachelor's in computer science (networks and telecoms)
    at HEH. It's my first job, and most of it has been building things on my own: SPARC from the
    first design to production, plus the platforms around it. Working alone taught me to keep
    systems simple, to test what matters, and to think about what happens when something fails,
    because when it breaks, the Teams message comes to me.
  </p>
  <p>
    Now I want to work in a team, with engineers I can learn from and review code with. I'm open to
    both backend and data engineering roles, and I'm getting deeper into streaming, CDC and
    lakehouses.
  </p>
  <p>
    Outside work, I'm building a small homelab on second-hand PCs, so I can break things there
    before I break them at work.
  </p>
  <p>
    I also gave a one-day training on AI for the common good to BELSPO, with the FARI AI Academy.
  </p>
  <p class="tags">{stackLine}</p>
</section>
